From ce6644ba7f40ac9436a9cc0bb2c30b69bf8f977a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Plecki <dylan@andyl.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:10:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add bounded supplied-stack pthread storage and terminal
 return

Add an explicit strict interface backed by a caller-retained physical arena. Route thread DTV, dynamic TLS, extra TSD, destructor nodes and priority bookkeeping through enforced finite requests, retaining canonical birth and physical-return facts.

Use nonwaiting registry and terminal lock attempts, preserve joined threads with outstanding cleanup debt, reject retained-span aliases and stale incarnations, and refuse unsupported heap and per-thread state producers before their ordinary paths.

Build the complete library with one compiler lane and a two-GiB per-process address-space ceiling. The real bounded controls and eleven targeted ordinary regressions pass. Nineteen ABI checks pass; libc check-abi retains the documented private-prefix LOCALEDIR data-size mismatch. Creation, TLS lookup, user callbacks and arbitrary caller profiles remain explicitly unqualified for nonwaiting execution.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Plecki <dylan@andyl.com>
