--- a/nptl/README.bounded-pthread
+++ b/nptl/README.bounded-pthread
@@ -252,6 +252,13 @@ state: tcache and thread_arena remain NULL, resolver and RPC state remain
 empty, and TLS/error buffers remain NULL.  The no-state cleanup path reaches
 no ordinary allocator or allocator global lock.
 
+Allocation and release share one actual nonwaiting allocation try-lock.
+Signal-handler release reentry refuses with sticky cleanup debt instead of
+reading a partially constructed header or releasing a node twice.  Release
+validates alignment and the complete header and payload span before reading
+nominated metadata.  Asynchronous signal-handler allocation remains outside
+the supported caller profile; this lock cut limits damage from reentry.
+
 Invalid, foreign or duplicate arena-node release also sets sticky
 cleanup_blocked debt.  Equal allocated/released counters alone cannot return
 backing after an uncertain TLS pointer release.  Terminal code withholds
@@ -294,7 +301,9 @@ exact per-kind final logical release; same-backing reuse with a new
 incarnation; stale-incarnation refusal; and fatal dynamic TLS exhaustion
 rather than heap fallback; strict allocator/resolver/error refusals;
 foreign-free retained debt; unexpected exit-tail state; raw kernel exit;
-and independent-owner output alias rejection preserving live stack bytes.
+and independent-owner output alias rejection preserving live stack bytes;
+actual signal-handler release at a held allocation lock; duplicate release;
+and malformed alignment, prefix, endpoint and payload-size refusal.
 These are implementation controls, not a complete
 application profile or proof for an unexecuted platform.
 
